welcome to another famous friday where  we look at how you can learn  from successful entrepreneurs and apply  what made them successful  to your business today's lesson is  care okay this might be a novel concept  for a lot of businesses but  you have to actually care about the  people who work for you  about your customers about your  community if you care about them then  guess what  they're gonna care about you and they're  going to give you more business they're  going to give you more money they're  going to refer more customers to you  if you actually care about them this  isn't that hard a strategy  one of my favorite entrepreneurs is  milton hershey there's so many great  reasons to love milton hershey but the  story i want to share with you today is  about how he really  cared about his team and his community  in 1929 the great depression hit  and everybody was laying people off was  firing people right they're trying to  save money save on costs and that just  made everything worse because now more  people didn't have jobs  milton hershey who founded hershey  chocolate said you know what i want to  be the change i want to  i want to try to kick start something i  think this is a great opportunity to  care about our community  and he decided to hire people to start a  community  works project that had nothing to do  with chocolate he started  hiring people to build a school to build  a sports arena to build a rec center and  to build a hotel  like what does that have to do with  chocolate  nothing but he's contributing to his  community and that's going to help his  company grow  and there's one famous story where he  was building his hotel  and somebody comes to him and say hey  milton you know we can uh  we've discovered this new shovel and  it's called a steam shovel and it can do  the work of 40 men  you can build your hotel so much faster  and he told the guy  forget the shovel hire the 40 men  because that was the whole point of this  project was to create jobs  and create a sense of community again  and uplift people's spirits  and you may be thinking well that's a  stupid decision  he could have he could have saved money  on those 40 jobs and you're thinking  short term you're playing the small game  where milton hershey understood that he  had to play a bigger game and that's the  long game and you have to care  and caring will often mean that you know  what  it may not make the most sense in a  short-term decision  but you can bet that those 40 people  will be loyal to milton hershey  forever and you can bet that their  friends and their family will be loyal  to milton hershey  forever and buy his products and rave  about his company  and the community that he built all  those things for will love milton  hershey  forever and now 2014  almost a century later i'm making a  video about it and other people are  still talking about it and this legend  and this story of milton hershey  continues to perpetuate how much value  has that added  to the hershey company and their bottom  line  way more than the cost of those 40 jobs  their salaries so you have to care  tap into your heart think about the  people who work for you  think about the customers who buy from  you think about the community that  you're part of  and do something today to show that you  actually  care about them because if you care  about them  they'll care about you believe  for those you watching like the video  you can subscribe to the channel to see  more videos  just like this thank you so much i'll  see you soon
 

